<p><a href="index.html"><img style="vertical-align: middle; " src="../../images/navtop.png"/></a> <a href="index.html">Contents</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="mysqlprototls.html"><img style="vertical-align: middle; " src="../../images/navprev.png"/></a> <a href="mysqlprototls.html">MySQL TLS/SSL Encryption and Authentication</a> | <a href="mysqlprotocol.html"><img style="vertical-align: middle; " src="../../images/navtop.png"/></a> <a href="mysqlprotocol.html">MySQL Protocol</a> | <a href="mysqlprotospecialpurpose.html">MySQL Special-Purpose Options</a> <a href="mysqlprotospecialpurpose.html"><img style="vertical-align: middle; " src="../../images/navnext.png"/></a></p>

<a name="mysqlforeignbackend"/><h1>Foreign Backend</h1>

<p>Since SQL Relay supports a variety of database back-ends, the app can also be redirected to any of these databases, instead of the MySQL/MariaDB database it was originally written to use.</p>

<p>This is as simple as specifying a different database using the <i>dbase</i> attribute in the instance tag and specifying the appropriate database connection string in the <i>string</i> attribute of the connection tag.</p>

<blockquote>
<!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight 3.1.9
by Lorenzo Bettini
http://www.lorenzobettini.it
http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
<pre><tt><b><font color="#000080">&lt;?xml</font></b> <font color="#009900">version</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"1.0"</font><b><font color="#000080">?&gt;</font></b>
<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;instances&gt;</font></b>
	<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;instance</font></b> <font color="#009900">id</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"example"</font> <font color="#009900">dbase</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"oracle"</font><b><font color="#0000FF">&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;listeners&gt;</font></b>
			<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;listener</font></b> <font color="#009900">protocol</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"mysql"</font> <font color="#009900">port</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"3306"</font><b><font color="#0000FF">/&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/listeners&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;connections&gt;</font></b>
			<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;connection</font></b> <font color="#009900">string</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"user=scott;password=tiger;oracle_sid=ora1"</font><b><font color="#0000FF">/&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/connections&gt;</font></b>
	<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/instance&gt;</font></b>
<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/instances&gt;</font></b>
</tt></pre>

</blockquote>
<p>In this example, a MySQL front-end provides MySQL/MariaDB applications access to an Oracle back-end database.</p>

<p>Depending on the back-end, it might also be necessary to make some other configuration changes, as well, for example:</p>

<ul>
  <li>In the instance tag:</li>
  <ul>
    <li>set translatebindvariables="yes"</li>
    <li>set the isolationlevel attribute</li>
    <li>set transactionmodel="explicit-deferred" - the transaction model that an app written for MySQL/MariaDB would expect</li>
  </ul>

  <li>In the string attribute of the connection tag:</li>
  <ul>
    <li>set autocommit=yes or autocommit=no</li>
    <li>implement a function that returns the last insert id and specify it using the lastinsertidfunction parameter</li>
    <li>set the identity parameter to override the database type</li>
    <li>set ignorespace=yes</li>
    <li>set the overrideschema parameter</li>
    <li>set the typemangling and/or tablemangling parameters - when using a PostgreSQL back-end</li>
  </ul>

  <li>use <a href="querytranslation.html#querytranslation">Query Translation</a> modules</li>
  <li>use <a href="resultsettranslation.html#resultsettranslation">Result Set Translation</a> modules</li>
  <li>use <a href="errortranslation.html#errortranslation">Error Translation</a> modules</li>
  <li>use <a href="sessionqueries.html#sessionqueries">Session Queries</a></li>
  <li>use one of the <a href="mysqlprotospecialpurpose.html">Special-Purpose Options</a></li>
</ul>

<p>If <a href="querytranslation.html#querytranslation">Query Translations</a> aren't sufficient, then it might still be necessary to modify some queries to use the syntax of the foreign database, or even update some code, but a full rewrite of the app should not be necessary.</p>

